# Swing visual parity

The React app in `frontend/` is a **desktop KeyStore Explorer**, not a marketing site or admin dashboard. Match the Swing chrome. Behavior stays YAML/`e2e-contract.mdc`; this rule is layout and look.

Read [`.cursor/discovery/UI.md`](../discovery/UI.md) and `kse/src/main/java/org/kse/gui/KseFrame.java` before adding or restyling screens. Optional: run Swing via the `build-and-run-locally` skill.

## Do

- Menubar: File, Edit, View, Tools, Examine, Help. The File slice renders **all** in-scope items (disabled until a feature registers). Out-of-scope items stay disabled.
- Toolbar under the menubar: icon groups (New/Open/Save, generate/import, …) with separators
- Empty state: Quick Start pane until a keystore tab is open
- Open stores: tab-per-keystore; selected tab owns the entry table
- Entry table: type, lock, expiry status, alias, algorithm, key size, cert expiry, last modified (`data-testid` = `keystore.table`)
- Dialogs as **modals** over the frame (password, alias, generate, details), not full-page routes
- Light desktop chrome: system-like fonts, gray toolbar, table in a bordered scroll pane
- Keep accessible names and `data-testid`s from `functional-tests/control-ids.md`

## Do not

- Invent a landing page, sidebar app-shell, card grid, or shadcn/Tailwind “product” look
- Dark mode, brand palettes, or marketing typography unless a human asks
- Pixel-match Metal/Windows L&F or native OS menus (Look-and-Feel prefs are out of scope)
- Drop the menubar in favor of icon-only navigation
- Name React components after Swing widgets (`JButton`, `DGetPassword`)

`modernize` may refactor component structure. It must **not** restyle away from this chrome.
